Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.64,0:00:21.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good luck with that, soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.48,0:00:38.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can smell the Ishbalan stray dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.56,0:00:39.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.53,0:00:42.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he's gone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.37,0:00:47.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.07,0:00:49.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what's going to happen to Marcoh-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.83,0:00:52.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer said he was going to look after him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.30,0:00:55.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What can we do about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.12,0:01:08.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}The Central Library?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.63,0:01:14.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san had to hide all of his materials right under the military's nose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.08,0:01:16.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And this...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.34,0:01:19.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}What do you suppose that means?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.74,0:01:20.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.45,0:01:24.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, let's keep this a secret from the Colonel and the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.65,0:01:25.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.76,0:01:28.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whether or not we can trust them anymore...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.03,0:01:31.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.10,0:01:36.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.82,0:01:41.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.10,0:01:46.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.85,0:01:53.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.53,0:03:30.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're leaving so suddenly?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.48,0:03:34.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm. Now that we know that Scar is in East City,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.03,0:03:37.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,everyone seems to have become \Nworried about Central all of a sudden.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.22,0:03:40.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry to have inconvenienced you, \Nbut we're going back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.32,0:03:42.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Before you do, \Nwhat is your punishment?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.82,0:03:44.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Punishment?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.47,0:03:48.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew where the Crystal Alchemist was, \Nand yet I left him alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.08,0:03:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've done well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.08,0:03:57.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanted to place him in protective custody.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.78,0:04:01.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The officer directly underneath me—\NGrand—was against it,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.67,0:04:06.55,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,but he put his research to use on the battlefield, which must have tormented him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.55,0:04:10.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At this late date, I would like to make it up to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.57,0:04:13.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, concerning his research...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.32,0:04:14.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That will be all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.85,0:04:17.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will continue to rely on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.05,0:04:22.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,May you have a safe journey.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.45,0:04:29.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.33,0:04:31.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,does not exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.88,0:04:36.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see, I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.70,0:04:44.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'd probably shape up \Nif you did get punished once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.88,0:04:47.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He never seems to \Nlet his guard down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.42,0:04:54.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Creation follows destruction!
Dialogue: 1,0:04:54.10,0:04:58.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I shall fix you up nice and pretty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.84,0:05:02.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-That's all right...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.49,0:05:05.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The method of bonding a soul to armor...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.22,0:05:08.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is only known by one person:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.49,0:05:10.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.01,0:05:16.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and for that to happen, I first \Nneed to do something about my arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.46,0:05:20.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're right. After all, if Edward-kun is unable to use his alchemy...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.71,0:05:23.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...he's just a sharp-tongued brat.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.59,0:05:29.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyhow, I'm going to my mechanic.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.80,0:05:31.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, you know who, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.08,0:05:37.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. I saw our good-for-nothing alchemist there once, bawling in pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.77,0:05:42.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"It hurts! It hurts so bad! \NI'm going to pee my pants!" Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.99,0:05:48.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you going to do once you're fixed up?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.46,0:05:51.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.07,0:05:53.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's something I want to look up in the library there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.83,0:05:56.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's going to be a long trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.93,0:05:57.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.38,0:06:01.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since I'm part of the Führer's party, I won't be able to accompany you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.14,0:06:05.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't very well leave here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.76,0:06:07.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I have to \Nkeep an eye on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.38,0:06:12.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't think I'd be able to protect \Nthose two from such a dangerous guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.80,0:06:14.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That goes for me too!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.16,0:06:16.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That settles it, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.77,0:06:21.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I shall escort these two during their journey!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.94,0:06:24.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't need that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.76,0:06:27.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you going to do if Scar \Nattacks you again in your condition?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.50,0:06:32.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't carry Al \Nlike that either, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.20,0:06:40.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Children should listen to adults.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.63,0:06:44.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-You're calling us children?! Al, say something!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.09,0:06:49.09,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Brother! This is the first time anyone has ever treated me like a child since I got this body!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.01,0:06:53.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well, Edward Elric...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.57,0:06:56.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall we begin packing?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.60,0:07:11.64,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,This is the first time anyone has ever \Ntreated me like luggage since I got this body.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.82,0:07:15.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.93,0:07:20.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, newspaper? \NI've got tea as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.38,0:07:21.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shoo, shoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.54,0:07:23.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, I've got a message from Roy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.51,0:07:24.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From the Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.13,0:07:28.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Don't go dying under my command. \NIt's a pain having to deal with everything."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.71,0:07:29.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.53,0:07:34.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell him, "Roger. There's no way I'm going to die ahead of you, you grubby colonel."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.58,0:07:38.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And while you're at it, \Ntake this escort with you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.42,0:07:39.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, now...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.83,0:07:45.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what Marcoh told you,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.28,0:07:46.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but let me inform you of one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.70,0:07:48.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Three years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.93,0:07:52.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we discovered the body of a young girl who had been transmuted into a Chimera.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.24,0:07:53.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nina?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.85,0:07:56.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The way she was torn apart...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.80,0:08:00.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It turns out to be identical to Scar's method of alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.35,0:08:09.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.02,0:08:13.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now I can take him on.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.97,0:08:20.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll see you in Central. I'll apply for permission to browse at the first branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.85,0:08:23.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll have to excuse me for using my left hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.38,0:08:30.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central... Central's first... \Nfirst something-or-other!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.53,0:08:32.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central Library, First Branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.86,0:08:34.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.52,0:08:35.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's enough, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.99,0:08:40.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.60,0:08:42.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.76,0:09:01.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the Führer... \NWhat is the Führer's answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.12,0:09:17.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You told that boy where your materials are hidden, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.62,0:09:19.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.63,0:09:21.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.42,0:09:24.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The boy will come even closer to the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.39,0:09:26.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I would be a little upset
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.18,0:09:30.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if you wrote down anything extra in those materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.90,0:09:36.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The boy is smart. Once he reads it, he won't do as you want him to.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.72,0:09:40.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is why, before he does,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.65,0:09:43.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought I'd look into it myself, you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.23,0:09:45.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That won't be possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.72,0:09:48.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to die...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.71,0:09:50.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.52,0:10:02.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was cruel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.73,0:10:05.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've already died once, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.81,0:10:12.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.82,0:10:15.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just like the stories say, \Nyou guys are...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.76,0:10:17.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.88,0:10:22.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell me...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.77,0:10:27.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Where did you tell the boy you hid your materials?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.12,0:10:34.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whew, I've had it, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.47,0:10:38.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy just keeps \Ngoing on and on,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.09,0:10:41.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and all he does is brag about his family background.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.23,0:10:43.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me take a break here—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.01,0:10:45.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.08,0:10:46.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? {\alpha&HFF&}Al? Al? Al? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.93,0:10:47.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al? {\alpha&HFF&}Al? Al? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.83,0:10:48.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al? Al? {\alpha&HFF&}Al? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.71,0:10:49.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al? Al? Al? {\alpha&HFF&}Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.47,0:10:50.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al? Al? Al? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.14,0:10:51.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.23,0:10:56.70,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Al got mistaken for someone else's luggage and was dropped off at the last station!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.70,0:10:59.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hm? That won't do. We'll go back for him at the next station.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.72,0:11:01.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't wait that long!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.09,0:11:02.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, now...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.33,0:11:04.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay out of my way!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.64,0:11:08.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Calm down, Edward Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.95,0:11:12.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What else could I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.58,0:11:17.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I, a suit of armor, said "not here," they would just be stunned by me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.77,0:11:21.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if Brother has noticed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.12,0:11:27.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm{\i0} the one who wants to cry, here!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.12,0:11:29.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.13,0:11:49.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He wouldn't have gone off somewhere by himself!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.20,0:11:52.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.53,0:11:53.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it was this armor?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.90,0:11:55.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.00,0:11:56.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're good at drawing, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.69,0:11:59.85,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It's a technique for drawing likenesses that has been passed down in my family for generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.85,0:12:01.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can you be \Ntaking this so lightly?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.05,0:12:04.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait, it's too dangerous! \NWhat's the hurry?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.20,0:12:07.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys just don't understand us!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.20,0:12:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.38,0:12:10.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard from Doctor Marcoh!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.43,0:12:12.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About what happened in Ishbal!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.32,0:12:46.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, do you know anything about some armor that was at the train station?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.57,0:12:48.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like who might've taken it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.78,0:12:50.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was large and dark...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.79,0:12:53.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a second, please!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.68,0:13:08.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ee-yow...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.34,0:13:18.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey! Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.04,0:13:24.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.33,0:13:26.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, I tell you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.87,0:13:34.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn. If I had my arm and leg, this wouldn't be so hard...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.56,0:14:00.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is trouble... We're getting farther \Nand farther away from the train station.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.67,0:14:03.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ahem...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.50,0:14:06.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Am I hearing things?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.86,0:14:09.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm right here. This armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.43,0:14:21.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That didn't hurt at all! With this...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.35,0:14:23.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.00,0:14:24.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's doing it again!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.09,0:14:27.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't be startled. I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.24,0:14:29.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.34,0:14:31.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the latest model of armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.07,0:14:35.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're popular now in Central. Talking armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.58,0:14:37.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's your switch?! Be quiet!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.66,0:14:39.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, you can't turn me off.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.07,0:14:44.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just keep quiet, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.89,0:14:49.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, where are we going?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.50,0:14:50.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.95,0:14:52.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.73,0:14:56.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Boss Poe said that \Nif I wanted to be like him,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.75,0:14:59.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I should go rub out a guy or two.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.47,0:15:02.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So I told him that I would go \Nlay into the Damousha family,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.36,0:15:05.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who are always \Ninvading our territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.78,0:15:08.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I bring back one of \Ntheir heads like this,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.26,0:15:11.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then no one will treat me like a kid anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.43,0:15:14.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be accepted as the boss's right-hand-man!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.60,0:15:16.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll do it! I'll flatten them!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.74,0:15:20.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not, by any chance, going to go kill someone?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.11,0:15:28.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're some pretty good armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.62,0:15:32.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't even have to worry if they pull a gun on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.74,0:15:34.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why you're wearing me?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.73,0:15:36.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So it won't hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.23,0:15:40.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. As long as I'm not hurt, I can go all-out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.87,0:15:42.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's still going to hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.91,0:15:45.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? Are you a defective product?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.89,0:15:47.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure it will hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.63,0:15:48.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In your heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.73,0:15:52.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be silly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.89,0:15:56.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or would you rather you didn't feel pain in your heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.03,0:15:57.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Relax your arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.17,0:15:59.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.52,0:16:12.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the Cursed Farmer... I mean,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.52,0:16:12.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx75\fscy75\pos(355.5,470)}Nyoroi no Noroi
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.28,0:16:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Cursed Armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.28,0:16:15.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fscx75\fscy75\pos(380,470)}Noroi no Yoroi
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.48,0:16:17.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once you become one with me,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.46,0:16:22.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,your mind and body will never \Nfeel pain again, forever and ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.56,0:16:26.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.54,0:16:30.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Having been made to live alone together with an old man,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.12,0:16:34.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she was thinking of what was best for the future, in her own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.90,0:16:39.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So she was just hoping to make things easier for her grandpa, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.12,0:16:41.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You did pretty well \Nto have noticed this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.44,0:16:44.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't give you this,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.66,0:16:48.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but if you want, I could introduce you \Nto the engineer who made it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.64,0:16:51.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's got a sharp tongue \Nbut decent skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.75,0:16:55.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I appreciate the offer, \Nbut I don't need an artificial leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.75,0:16:58.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once you get used to it, \Nit's pretty handy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.87,0:17:01.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Perhaps so. However...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.87,0:17:06.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I'd like to leave my leg the way it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.58,0:17:17.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A sword wound I received on \Nthe battlefield became infected.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.91,0:17:21.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the time they carried me to the rear, all they could do was cut it off.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.31,0:17:24.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Battlefield... You were a soldier?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.10,0:17:27.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which war?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.08,0:17:28.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one up north?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.40,0:17:29.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.90,0:17:31.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't mean Ishbal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.86,0:17:37.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the battlefield, \Neveryone becomes some other creature.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.21,0:17:41.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can carry out even the most cruel acts without any feeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.84,0:17:47.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to protect myself, my mind must have shut out all emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.75,0:17:53.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But once the war is over, \Nyou can't keep doing that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.95,0:17:59.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I must not forget what I saw there... \Nwhat I did there.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.10,0:18:03.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I look at this injury, it allows me to remember it all immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.73,0:18:05.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And that's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.32,0:18:08.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why you don't want \Nany Automail?! That isn't very—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.38,0:18:10.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not the only reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.53,0:18:14.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lost my leg.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.28,0:18:19.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I have gained something even more important.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.16,0:18:24.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Peace of mind, and a life with my grandchildren. You see...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.15,0:18:32.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's once a person loses something \Nthat they first gain something, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.18,0:18:33.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.88,0:18:36.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are those who've \Ngone to war and come back fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.52,0:18:38.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what soldiers do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.72,0:18:42.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those people have lost something.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.73,0:18:45.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if it isn't something \Nvisible to the eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.20,0:18:53.15,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If you've lost something yourself, \Nthen you should've gained something as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.80,0:18:57.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In alchemy, that is what's known as equivalent exchange, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.51,0:19:04.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can that be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.71,0:19:10.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lost my right arm and left leg...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.07,0:19:13.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and my brother lost his whole body.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.41,0:19:18.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're living desperately just to get them back!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.80,0:19:20.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Taking everything back—
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.32,0:19:22.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that's what our dream is!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.00,0:19:26.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't a thing \Nwe've gained in return!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.85,0:19:28.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everything...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.77,0:19:30.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,has been taken from us!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.39,0:19:40.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A dream to take everything back...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.16,0:19:43.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, once that comes true, \Nwhat will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.80,0:19:49.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A dream that is granted can't be called a real dream at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.93,0:20:13.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.88,0:20:17.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, we're going to take it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.51,0:20:20.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks for the tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.91,0:20:47.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.49,0:20:50.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, Brother is home!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.24,0:20:52.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's right! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.89,0:20:53.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.92,0:20:55.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.83,0:20:58.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.91,0:21:04.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.38,0:21:06.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you reek of sheep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.31,0:21:12.03,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Well, excuse me! Fine, when we get to \NGrandma Pinako's house, I'll get washed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.44,0:21:15.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.34,0:21:18.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Four years ago, when the Colonel came to Resembool,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.88,0:21:22.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he said it was because he happened to look at the letter we sent out, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.92,0:21:24.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.86,0:21:26.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was searching for Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.08,0:21:32.45,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,But, by any chance, do you think the reason \Nthat the Colonel went to Granny's house was...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.75,0:21:36.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.64,0:21:39.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was worried about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.03,0:21:40.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.00,0:21:42.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.58,0:21:45.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.93,0:21:50.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about earlier...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.88,0:21:56.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.11,0:22:00.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we miss this one, we'll have to wait until tomorrow at noon!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.80,0:22:03.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hey! What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.32,0:22:03.96,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,We're going to run!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.96,0:22:05.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the method of \Nshort-distance sprinting
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.26,0:22:07.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that has been passed down \Nthrough my family for generations!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.28,0:22:11.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Put me down!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.28,0:22:11.05,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,I'm going to break!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.02,0:23:40.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.73,0:23:44.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 17: "House of the Waiting Family"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.18,0:23:45.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the day we left,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.72,0:23:47.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we burned down our house.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.05,0:23:50.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We had nowhere to return home to.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.71,0:23:52.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or so we thought...
